WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.400
-Enjoy yourself.
Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.734
Welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:08.067
You're here. You're watching.
"The Tonight Show" is on.

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:09.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.434
Hey, this is exciting.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.133
I want to say
congratulations to Disney

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:16.334
for celebrating their
100th anniversary today.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:18.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:20.467
100.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.734
And to celebrate 100 years,

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.501
ironically, pricing on Disney+

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:27.534
went from Goofy status
to this is ducking insane.

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:29.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:33.767
Of course, Disneyland's slogan
is the happiest place on Earth.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.667
It's not to be confused with
the slogan for Busch Gardens --

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:40.267
"technically a place on Earth,"
and you go, well, it is.

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:43.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:47.033
Well, get this. Rite Aid
just filed for bankruptcy

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:50.634
and could be closing more than
2,000 of their stores.

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:52.434
Yeah, it's amazing
that their business model

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:54.801
of just being a crappier
CVS didn't pan out.

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:56.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.467
But they actually pressed
the button for help weeks ago,

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:00.234
but no one noticed until now.

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:04.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.734
Meanwhile, Jada Pinkett Smith

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.234
said that they were bankrupt
seven years ago

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:08.734
but just didn't tell anyone.

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.300
It's interesting.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.167
[ Audience oohs ]

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.767
[ Rimshot ]

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.834
You could tell that they were
going out of business

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:19.300
when they just relabeled Tums
as Halloween candy.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.634
You go, "That's it."

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:22.367
You could tell that they were
going out of business

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:24.434
when you asked the pharmacist
what he had for pain,

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.000
and he handed you
his bottle of Cuervo.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:33.133
Some news from Washington.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:36.734
The House is coming up
on two weeks without a speaker,

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:39.601
and tomorrow Republicans
plan to hold a vote.

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:41.200
If the House can't
elect a speaker,

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.534
the Constitution says
that it will be decided

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:45.067
by the judges
on "The Masked Singer."

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:48.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.000
The speaker is now Disco Pickle.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.667
Now, Republicans and Democrats

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:56.601
are talking about a bipartisan
solution to finding a speaker.

00:01:56.601 --> 00:01:57.901
That's how crazy things
have gotten.

00:01:57.901 --> 00:01:59.434
Our government
is so dysfunctional

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:00.567
it might become functional.

00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:02.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:04.968
Well, some huge political news.
In his new biography,

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:07.801
Senator Mitt Romney
says that back in 2020,

00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:10.033
Oprah suggested that they run
for president

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:12.968
together to keep former
president Trump out of office.

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:14.367
Wow.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:18.067
If you thought Dr. Fauci was
confused, imagine Dr. Phil.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:19.667
"Of all the chicks
in the henhouse

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:22.000
trying to lay a golden egg,

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.234
and you're on the wrong side
of the beaver dam."

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:28.167
Can I go outside or...?

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:29.701
When he heard about
Romney and Oprah,

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:31.367
Trump was like,
"Get me Maury Povich."

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:33.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:35.567
"Two things. Run with me.

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.834
Number two, prove that
Eric is not my son.

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:40.801
I'm not the father. I'm not.
You all don't know me."

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:44.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:45.467
Speaking of running
for president,

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.834
I read that Mike Pence's
presidential campaign

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.767
is more than $600,000 in debt.

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:52.467
Yeah, instead of a plane,

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:55.367
he and his staff get around
on a five-person tandem bike.

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:57.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.601 --> 00:02:59.200
I knew Pence
was in money trouble

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.534
when he changed his campaign
slogan to "Mike Pence,

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.501
the Rite Aid
of Republican candidates."

00:03:03.501 --> 00:03:07.267
Yeah, that's when I knew.
-Yeah.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:09.400
-Hey, I saw that NBC News
is going to host

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.033
the third Republican
primary debate.

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:13.667
And since the debate
is on NBC,

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:15.267
all the moderators
will press a button

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.567
and spin their chairs around

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:17.667
when they hear
something they like.

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:20.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:23.300
Switching gears,
National Geographic is releasing

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.267
a "Top Gun"-inspired docu series

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:30.067
that will follow the journeys of
students at a Navy pilot school.

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:31.567
Yeah, that's a formula
for a hit.

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:34.834
"Top Gun" minus Tom Cruise
plus school. Awesome.

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:36.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.901 --> 00:03:39.200
Well, guys, it is Monday.
I thought it would be helpful

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.033
to say goodbye to everything
from the past week

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:42.801
and say hello to everything
that's coming up.

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:44.467
It's time for "Goodbye, Hello."

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:48.968
-♪ Goodbye, hello ♪

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:50.767
[ Applause ]

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:54.601
-Goodbye,
New York Comic-Con and hello,

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.100
Times Square Elmo
re-establishing

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.534
dominance over the city.

00:03:57.534 --> 00:04:01.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:05.033
Goodbye, Airbnb
allowing rentals in New York,

00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:07.200
and hello,
paying 2 grand a night

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.901
to sleep in the employee
break room at Gray's Papaya.

00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:13.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:16.601
Goodbye, quality,
affordable meals from Chipotle

00:04:16.601 --> 00:04:19.701
after you raised
your prices, and hello,

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:21.601
Chipotle being where you now
take your spouse

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:22.968
for your 20th anniversary.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:27.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.000
Goodbye, hidden junk fees
recently outlawed

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.534
by President Biden,

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:34.033
and hello, seeing everyone's
junk on the number-one

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:36.133
streaming show
"Naked Attraction."

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:38.033
[ Applause ]

00:04:38.033 --> 00:04:40.567
And finally, goodbye, Rite Aid

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:44.300
for declaring bankruptcy
on all 2,100 stores.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.267
Hello, 2,100 brand-new locations
of Spirit Halloween.

00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:50.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:52.234
When you move out,
they move in.

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:57.033
-♪ Goodbye, hello ♪

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:59.000
-Thank you very much.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.834
You guys see this? Ferrari
is now letting customers

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:05.868
in the U.S. buy their cars
with cryptocurrency.

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:07.133
It's perfect.

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:09.033
Now you can make two bad
financial decisions at once.

00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:11.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:14.501
Congratulations.

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:16.300
Yep. Crypto and your Ferrari.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:19.501
Two things no one wants
to hear you talk about.

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:21.767
Meanwhile, Kia will continue
to accept payment

00:05:21.767 --> 00:05:23.067
in Chuck E. Cheese tickets.

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:25.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:26.234
-Wow.

00:05:26.234 --> 00:05:27.734
-And finally, I heard
that United Airlines

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:30.100
is bringing back their boarding
process of travelers

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.968
with window seats
going first,

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:34.968
then middle seats,
and then aisle seats,

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:37.601
while Southwest will continue
their official boarding process,

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:38.801
every man for themselves.

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:40.634
We have a great show.

